## 🎨 Figure & Axes Architecture

### Creating Figures

**Single Plot:**
```python
# Most common
fig, ax = plt.subplots()
ax.plot(x, y)
```

**Multiple Subplots:**
```python
# Grid layout
fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3)  # 2 rows, 3 columns
# axes is 2D array: axes[i, j]

# 1D layout
fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1)  # 3 rows, 1 column
# axes is 1D array: axes[i]

# Single axis case
fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 1)  # Can use axes[0, 0] or treat as single
```

**Complex Layouts:**
```python
# GridSpec for unequal sizes
import matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec

fig = plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))
gs = gridspec.GridSpec(3, 3, figure=fig)

ax1 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, :])      # Top row, all columns
ax2 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1:, :-1])   # Bottom 2 rows, left 2 cols
ax3 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1:, -1])    # Bottom 2 rows, last col
```

**Figure Size & DPI:**
```python
# Size in inches (width, height)
fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))  # 10 inches wide, 6 tall

# DPI (dots per inch) - affects file size and quality
fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6), dpi=100)
# For print: 300 dpi, for screen: 100 dpi

# Default: figsize=(6.4, 4.8) at 100 dpi
```

### Axes Properties

**Limits:**
```python
ax.set_xlim(0, 10)      # Set x-axis limits
ax.set_ylim(-5, 5)      # Set y-axis limits

# Auto-scale with padding
ax.margins(0.1)         # 10% padding on all sides

# Get current limits
xmin, xmax = ax.get_xlim()
ymin, ymax = ax.get_ylim()
```

**Axis Scale:**
```python
# Linear (default)
ax.set_xscale('linear')

# Logarithmic (for wide-range data)
ax.set_xscale('log')

# Logit (for probabilities)
ax.set_xscale('logit')

# Symlog (symmetric log, good for data with +/-)
ax.set_xscale('symlog')
```

**Ticks and Labels:**
```python
# Set tick locations
ax.set_xticks([0, 5, 10, 15])
ax.set_yticks([0, 25, 50, 75, 100])

# Set tick labels
ax.set_xticklabels(['Low', 'Medium', 'High', 'Very High'])

# Rotate labels
ax.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)

# Scientific notation for large numbers
ax.ticklabel_format(style='sci', axis='y', scilimits=(0,0))

# Remove ticks
ax.set_xticks([])
```

**Grid:**
```python
# Enable grid
ax.grid(True)

# Customize grid
ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, linestyle='--', linewidth=0.5)

# Only show minor grid
ax.grid(True, which='minor', alpha=0.2)

# Remove grid
ax.grid(False)
```

**Spine Control:**
```python
# Remove spines (borders)
ax.spines['top'].set_visible(False)
ax.spines['right'].set_visible(False)

# Or remove all spines
for spine in ax.spines.values():
    spine.set_visible(False)

# Customize spine properties
ax.spines['bottom'].set_linewidth(2)
ax.spines['left'].set_color('red')
```

